ation a\nBreakpoint 3, main () at stackbugs.c:59\n59\t    printf(\"a: %d\\n\", a);\n#0  main () at stackbugs.c:59\nNo symbol \"i\" in current context.","status":"","stdout":"","summary":"watchpoint on a never fired: b[4] is not a here","verdict":"silent"}},"ubsan":{"fixed":{"cmd":"gcc -O0 -fno-stack-protector -fsanitize=undefined","report":"","status":"exit 0","stdout":"b[0]: 5\nb[1]: 5\nb[2]: 5\nb[3]: 5\nj: (nil)\na: 1\n","summary":"correct output, no reports","verdict":"ok"},"null":{"cmd":"gcc -O0 -fno-stack-protector -fsanitize=undefined -DBUG_NULL","report":"stackbugs.c:36:8: runtime error: store to null pointer of type 'int'","status":"signal SIGSEGV","stdout":"","summary":"UBSan: store to null pointer of type 'int'","verdict":"caught"},"oob":{"cmd":"gcc -O0 -fno-stack-protector -fsanitize=undefined -DBUG_OOB","report":"","status":"exit 0","stdout":"b[0]: 5\nb[1]: 5\nb[2]: 5\nb[3]: 5\nj: (nil)\na: 1\n","summary":"no symptom: output looks correct","verdict":"silent"}},"valgrind":{"fixed":{"cmd":"valgrind ./valgrind-fixed   # gcc -O0 -fno-stack-protector","report":"","status":"exit 0","stdout":"b[0]: 5\nb[1]: 5\nb[2]: 5\nb[3]: 5\nj: (nil)\na: 1\n","summary":"correct output, no reports","verdict":"ok"},"null":{"cmd":"valgrind ./valgrind-null   # gcc -O0 -fno-stack-protector -DBUG_NULL","report":"==PID== Invalid write of size 4\n==PID==    at 0x…: sub (stackbugs.c:36)\n==PID==    by 0x…: main (stackbugs.c:57)\n==PID==  Address 0x0 is not stack'd, malloc'd or (recently) free'd\n==PID== Process terminating with default action of signal 11 (SIGSEGV)\n==PID==  Access not within mapped region at address 0x0\n==PID==    at 0x…: sub (stackbugs.c:36)\n==PID==    by 0x…: main (stackbugs.c:57)","status":"signal SIGSEGV","stdout":"","summary":"Valgrind: invalid write of size 4 to address 0x0","verdict":"caught"},"oob":{"cmd":"valgrind ./valgrind-oob   # gcc -O0 -fno-stack-protector -DBUG_OOB","report":"","status":"exit 0","stdout":"b[0]: 5\nb[1]: 5\nb[2]: 5\nb[3]: 5\nj: (nil)\na: 1\n","summary":"no symptom: output looks correct","verdict":"silent"}}},"toolchain":{"clang":"Ubuntu clang version 18.1.3 (1ubuntu1)","gcc":"gcc (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1) 13.3.0","gdb":"GNU gdb (Ubuntu 15.1-1ubuntu1~24.04.1) 15.1","valgrind":"valgrind-3.22.0"}}},"rows":[["O0-plain","-O0, no protections"],["O0-default","-O0, toolchain defaults"],["gcc-O2","gcc -O2"],["clang-O0","clang -O0"],["clang-O2","clang -O2"],["asan","AddressSanitizer (-O0)"],["asan-O2","AddressSanitizer, clang -O2"],["ubsan","UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer"],["valgrind","Valgrind memcheck"],["safeheap","Emscripten SAFE_HEAP"],["gdb","gdb: backtrace / watchpoint on a"]],"source":"/*\n * stackbugs.c - two classic memory bugs, small enough to see every byte.\n *\n * Built normally this is the fixed program. Either bug can be compiled back\n * in, so every tool and platform can be tested against the real thing:\n *\n *   -DBUG_NULL   store through a NULL pointer\n *   -DBUG_OOB    the fill loop runs one step too far and writes b[LEN],\n *                one int past the end of main's array\n *\n * What each bug does depends on the platform, compiler and flags; see\n * docs/DESIGN.md. Output of the fixed program:\n *\n *   b[0]: 5\n *   b[1]: 5\n *   b[2]: 5\n *   b[3]: 5\n *   j: (nil)          (%p of a null pointer: glibc \"(nil)\", musl \"0\")\n *   a: 1\n */\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\n#include \"frame_hook.h\"\n\n#define LEN 4\n\nvoid sub(int b[]);\n\nvoid sub(int b[])\n{\n    int i;\n    int *j = NULL;\n\n#ifdef BUG_NULL\n    *j = 0;\n#endif\n    /* fill the caller's array with 5s */\n#ifdef BUG_OOB\n    for (i = 0; i <= LEN; i++)\n#else\n    for (i = 0; i < LEN; i++)\n#endif\n        b[i] = 5;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < LEN; i++)\n        printf(\"b[%d]: %d\\n\", i, b[i]);\n    printf(\"j: %p\\n\", (void *)j);\n}\n\nint main(void)\n{\n    int a = 1;\n    int b[LEN];\n\n    FRAME_HOOK(\"before\", &a, b);\n    sub(b);\n    FRAME_HOOK(\"after\", &a, b);\n    printf(\"a: %d\\n\", a);\n    return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n","static_rows":[["gcc-warn","gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra"],["gcc-nullderef","gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Wnull-dereference"],["gcc-analyzer","gcc -fanalyzer"],["clang-warn","clang -O2 -Wall -Wextra"],["clang-analyze","clang --analyze"],["cppcheck","cppcheck --enable=warning,portability"]],"wasm_rows":["O0-plain","O0-default","clang-O2","asan","asan-O2","ubsan","safeheap"]}
